{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118463","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118463/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118463/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118463/events","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118463","id":4246519122,"node_id":"I_kwDOAO6SJc79HL1S","number":118463,"title":"PhysicsServer*WrapMT::is_flushing_queries() and get_process_info() bypass command queue (race condition)","user":{"login":"rayamazaky","id":238893411,"node_id":"U_kgDODj05Yw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/238893411?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rayamazaky","html_url":"https://github.com/rayamazaky","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rayamazaky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rayamazaky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rayamazaky/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rayamazaky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rayamazaky/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rayamazaky/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rayamazaky/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rayamazaky/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rayamazaky/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","color":"ff6055","default":true,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":370471880,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzNzA0NzE4ODA=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:physics","name":"topic:physics","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-12T04:28:07Z","updated_at":"2026-04-13T09:17:15Z","closed_at":"2026-04-13T09:16:46Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: 4.7.dev\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen physics runs on a separate thread (`create_thread == true`), most methods in `PhysicsServer2DWrapMT` and `PhysicsServer3DWrapMT` use command queues to safely dispatch calls to the physics thread. However, `is_flushing_queries()` and `get_process_info()` bypass this mechanism and directly call the contained physics server:\n\n**physics_server_2d_wrap_mt.h:323-329:**\n```cpp\nvirtual bool is_flushing_queries() const override {\n    return physics_server_2d->is_flushing_queries();\n}\n\nint get_process_info(ProcessInfo p_info) override {\n    return physics_server_2d->get_process_info(p_info);\n}\n```\n\n**physics_server_3d_wrap_mt.h:406-412:**\n```cpp\nvirtual bool is_flushing_queries() const override {\n    return physics_server_3d->is_flushing_queries();\n}\n\nint get_process_info(ProcessInfo p_info) override {\n    return physics_server_3d->get_process_info(p_info);\n}\n```\n\nThis creates a data race: the calling thread reads state that the physics thread may be concurrently modifying. This violates the thread safety model established by the rest of the WrapMT class.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Enable threaded physics in project settings.\n2. Call `is_flushing_queries()` or `get_process_info()` from the main thread during physics processing.\n3. Potential torn reads or inconsistent state.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A — race condition visible from comparing these methods with the rest of the WrapMT class which uses command queues.","closed_by":{"login":"rsubtil","id":6501975,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDE5NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6501975?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil","html_url":"https://github.com/rsubtil","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118463/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118463/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"not_planned","pinned_comment":null}